\&\f(CW\*(C`binom_test\*(C'\fR was cross\-validated against R 4.6.1 \f(CW\*(C`stats::binom.test\*(C'\fR and SciPy
1.17.1 \f(CW\*(C`scipy.stats.binomtest\*(C'\fR using their own test suites rather than cases
invented here: SciPy\*(Aqs \f(CW\*(C`TestBinomTest\*(C'\fR, R\*(Aqs \f(CW\*(C`binom.test(c(800,10))\*(C'\fR from
\&\f(CW\*(C`tests/reg\-tests\-2.R\*(C'\fR, the \f(CW\*(C`?binom.test\*(C'\fR example, and an R\-generated corpus of
383 p\-values and 1560 Clopper\-Pearson bounds. They are in
\&\f(CW\*(C`t/binom_test.R.scipy.t\*(C'\fR. Two fixes came out of it, both in the incomplete beta
that every tail and confidence bound goes through:
.IP \(bu 4
Its continued fraction stopped after a flat 500 terms, but it needs about
0.25 sqrt(a+b) of them once the shape parameters are large, so it was quietly
cut short at big \f(CW\*(C`n\*(C'\fR: \f(CW\*(C`binom_test(10079990, 21000000, p => 0.48)\*(C'\fR returned
0.996781946606 where R and SciPy both give 0.9966892187965, i.e. wrong in the
fourth decimal of a printed p\-value. The cap now scales with sqrt(a+b), and
the front factor moved off differenced \f(CW\*(C`lgamma\*(C'\fR onto the same saddle\-point
form \f(CW\*(C`dbinom\*(C'\fR already used here. Agreement with R over these cases went from
9.3e\-5 to 3.3e\-13 relative.
.IP \(bu 4
The Clopper\-Pearson bounds are found by bisection, which stopped at an
absolute width of 1e\-15, so a bound far below 1 came back with only four
correct digits: \f(CW\*(C`binom\e_test(1, 1000000000, alternative => \*(Aqgreater\*(Aq,
conf\e_level => 0.999)\*(C'\fR gave 1.00053299e\-12 against R\*(Aqs 1.00050033e\-12. The
stopping rule is now relative to where the bracket sits, and such bounds now
hold about 1e\-15.
.PP
Both fixes also help \f(CW\*(C`t_test\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`var_test\*(C'\fR and \f(CW\*(C`cor_test\*(C'\fR, which use the same
function. One limit remains, pinned by the tests rather than left to chance: the
upper bound for a handful of successes in a billion trials still carries about
1e\-9 of relative error, because the complement branch of the incomplete beta
cannot resolve a tiny \f(CW\*(C`x\*(C'\fR past the spacing of \f(CW\*(C`1\-x\*(C'\fR.
